  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the speed of the block be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. Then from conservation of momentum, the velocity of the cylinder will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math> in the opposite direction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Now from conservation of energy<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br />so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>3&nbsp;</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
